Consequently, our strategy for engaging in locally powered, data-driven development starts with acknowledging four potential gaps:
Gap 1: Local expertise to frame locally relevant development questions Gap 2: Consistent production of high-quality data through carefully designed experiments, studies, or surveys at the international, national, and local levels


